From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:03:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 27/44] render: colorn tints particles the way Wallpaper Engine
 does
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`instanceoverride.colorn` multiplied every particle's colour in RGB, so a
coloured system was darkened instead of re-hued, and a colorn equal to
the system's own colour tinted it again (red on red). WE 2.8.485:

- Each system has a reference colour (GH 0x1401f2210): the mid-point of
  its first colorrandom's min and max (÷255), else its first
  colorchange's startvalue, else white with no colour source.
- colorn tints only when the object sets it, the particle flags lack 8,
  and it differs from the reference by 0.9/255 or more in some channel
  (GH 0x140251f70).
- The tint is an HSV shift (patch op 0xb in GH 0x1401ff240): colorrandom's
  min and max move by (colorn − reference) in hue (wrapped; a colour with
  s < 0.01 takes colorn's hue), saturation and value (clamped to 0..1).
  A system without a colour source spawns at colorn instead (template
  flag 0x200000).

The tint is re-evaluated every step, so a colorn bound to a user
property, a script or an animation is live.

Origin: ours
Why: wrong particle hues in 43 of the owner's scenes (docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B3: P5)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01288H8YtBieDNWXo3bvfKaP
